1712	1772	1709	1710	his wife	24	“ I am sorry to hear _ that _ ; but why did you not tell me so before ? If I had known as much this morning , I certainly would not have called on him . It is very unlucky ; but as I have actually paid the visit , we can not escape the acquaintance now . ”
1818	1891	1803	1803	she	13	“ How good it was in you , my dear Mr. Bennet ! But I knew I should persuade you at last . I was sure you loved your girls too well to neglect such an acquaintance . Well , how pleased I am ! And it is such a good joke , too , that you should have gone this morning , and never said a word about it till now . ”
1892	1906	1908	1909	Mr. Bennet	3	“ Now , Kitty , you may cough as much as you choose , ”
